WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:06.262
First: a G C C tenant is
read on which Graph host?

3
00:00:06.262 --> 00:00:11.401
The answer is c: graph dot microsoft
dot com, the worldwide endpoint.

4
00:00:11.401 --> 00:00:17.437
GCC High and DoD have their own hosts,
but G C C keeps the worldwide one.

5
00:00:17.437 --> 00:00:22.500
Second: M C nine hundred thousand and
three is action required with no date.

6
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.188
Why?

7
00:00:23.188 --> 00:00:24.413
The answer is b.

8
00:00:24.413 --> 00:00:27.821
The kit's rule marks a
prevent-or-fix-issue post without

9
00:00:27.821 --> 00:00:31.001
a date as action required,
and labels the basis rule.

10
00:00:31.001 --> 00:00:34.525
Microsoft didn't set a date,
and the kit doesn't make one up.

11
00:00:34.525 --> 00:00:36.952
The module page has three more questions,

12
00:00:36.952 --> 00:00:39.500
each linked to the
section that answers it.
